<p>&nbsp;</p>
<h2>Welcome to the CARMEN version 1.0!</h2>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Carmen is a framework to develop PGM (Probabilistic Graphical
Models).</p>
<p>The main difference Carmen will offer to you&nbsp;against other
PGM projects is the main emphasis that has been done to follow the
Software Engineering Principles.The main advantange which have been
achieved following those principles is a full documentation project with
specifications and design documents, so there are less errors, it is
becoming more efficient, more maintainable and, as a final consequence,
it will be easy to make new contributions by a totally new member of the
Carmen project team.</p>
<p>The Carmen application screen is divided into two main panes. The
tabs on the upper side provide navigation within Camen application. You
can double click a menu or an icon on the upper side in order&nbsp;to
open the corresponding dialog or working area on the bottom side. On the
graphical items on the network, you can double click to open their
corresponding properties dialog.</p>
<p>Network will always maintain their integrity as you
add/modify/delete elements and/or you apply an algorithm.</p>
<h3>Open / Write networks</h3>
<p>Carmen allows to open networks coming from Elvira, Huggin and
Carmen formats and allows to write networks on Elvira and Carmen
formats, so you can use also Carmen for converting networks from one
format to another.</p>
<p>The design is made to allow different formats to be incorporated
easily.</p>
<h3>Other Features and Online Help</h3>
<p>Carmen offers lots of other features.&nbsp; Please explore the
these features on the toolbar and menus.</p>
<p>Complete online help is available under the Help menu, with
Contents and Searching engines both for final end users and for
technical users.</p>
<p>"F1" key is also provided on the major topics around the
different dialog boxes of the project.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<h2><u>Thank you for using CARMEN&nbsp;and... enjoy it!!!</u></h2>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
